=== 5. token cost of the note (claim: ~25 prompt tokens) ===
  n=54 notes, chars min/median/max = 341/345/356
  ~chars/4 tokens: median 86, i.e. 3.5x the stated 25 tokens

=== 6. upside/downside ledger of shipping the gated note ===
  abs firings on questions ALREADY correct (no upside, possible no-op): 11
  abs firings on actual losses (max upside):                          1 ['a96c20ee_abs']
  answerable firings on ALREADY-CORRECT answers (downside exposure):  33
  answerable firings already wrong (nothing to lose):                 9
  of the 33 at-risk correct answers, how many already decline? 1 -> the model currently does NOT treat term-absence as a reason to refuse
  break-even flip rate on the at-risk set: 3.0% (above this the note is net-negative on judge accuracy over 500)

=== 7. robustness: can ANY threshold of this family reach gate-worthy precision? ===
